{"type":"message","id":"316d9c16","parentId":"7798cb99","timestamp":"2026-04-24T10:17:29.308Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering failure handling**\n\nI’m thinking about how to handle a tool failure and whether I should use my self-improvement skills here. The instructions mention utilizing those skills when something fails unexpectedly. But do I really need to select a specific skill? Hmm, maybe it’s not necessary, and I should just keep going. I could leverage Python 3 for whatever needs to be done next. Alright, let’s proceed!\n\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_RzQGJsVEUQbLeh4OPh3Y6z9H","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"set -e\nLATEST_JSON=$(curl -sSL \"https://api.github.com/repos/okx/onchainos-skills/releases/latest\" || true)\nLATEST_TAG=$(printf '%s' \"$LATEST_JSON\" | python3 - <<'PY'\nimport sys, json\ns=sys.stdin.read().strip()\nif not s:\n    print(\"\")\nelse:\n    try:\n        print(json.loads(s).get('tag_name',''))\n    except Exception:\n        print(\"\")\nPY\n)\nif ! command -v onchainos >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"ONCHAINOS_MISSING\"\n  echo \"LATEST_TAG=$LATEST_TAG\"\n  exit 0\nfi\nmkdir -p ~/.onchainos\nNEED_INSTALL=0\nif [ ! -f ~/.onchainos/last_check ]; then\n  NEED_INSTALL=1\nelse\n  NOW=$(date +%s)\n  LAST=$(cat ~/.onchainos/last_check 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n  AGE=$((NOW - LAST))\n  if [ \"$AGE\" -gt 43200 ]; then NEED_INSTALL=1; fi\nfi\necho \"LATEST_TAG=$LATEST_TAG\"\necho \"NEED_INSTALL=$NEED_INSTALL\"\nonchainos --version\n","workdir":"/home/zbb/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"custom","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":571,"output":416,"cacheRead":38912,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":39899,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777025838342,"responseId":"resp_02910bdb63f581f00169eb4330ce1481919bf1cf43c2a37541"}}
