{"type":"message","id":"bf9903cf","parentId":"bcf1c399","timestamp":"2026-04-24T10:26:05.501Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering reminder setup**\n\nI think I need to set up a cron reminder for the user, who wants to monitor KAT until midnight. A recurring cron job every 15 or 30 minutes could work well. I should also consider user-specific thresholds, but they mentioned pinning until midnight, which likely means I can set it up based on that. I’ll need to remind them it’ll ping during notable moves, so I should plan a job for every 15 minutes. However, I need to think about how to handle the end time.\n\n**Evaluating monitoring setup**\n\nI’m considering whether to use a one-shot at midnight to stop the monitoring, but that might be too complicated. Instead, I could set a cron job for every 15 minutes and include a stop condition to monitor until midnight. This might work better with session continuity. The user needs the monitoring until midnight, so I’ll create a cron job to disable it at that time. However, I need to think about how to set an end time since otherwise, it could run indefinitely.\n\n**Creating cron expression**\n\nI need to establish the current date from metadata—April 24, 2026, in Asia/Shanghai. It looks like I can create a cron expression to run every 15 minutes today until 23:45. I might use \"30,45 18 * * *\" for the times at 18:30 and 18:45, and then \"0,15,30,45 19-23 * * *\" for the hours from 19:00 to 23:45. This should adequately set up reminders for today within the standard cron format!\n\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"我给你挂到今晚 12 点，按 15 分钟巡一次；如果接近我们刚才盯的关键位，就直接提醒你。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mXneugVeLBcpO8DHpg0SN1ES","name":"cron","arguments":{"action":"add","job":{"name":"KAT monitor 2026-04-24 18:30","schedule":{"kind":"cron","expr":"30,45 18 24 4 *","tz":"Asia/Shanghai"},"payload":{"kind":"agentTurn","message":"监控 Base 链 KAT（Katana，合约地址 0xd53